This black hole is so big our entire solar system would fit across it 27 times. TON 618 weighs around 40 billion Suns, shines brighter than thousands of galaxies, and grew so fast that it shouldn’t exist. But the scariest part is what would happen to you if you fell in.

In this video:

TON 618 vs Sagittarius A*, the black hole at the centre of our galaxy;
why it shines like 140 trillion Suns;
the light that left it 10.8 billion years ago;
why scientists can’t explain how it grew so big so fast;
the glowing gas cloud three times wider than the Milky Way;
what would happen if TON 618 replaced our Sun;
what you would feel crossing its edge, and how long you would have left.

Would you take the jump? Tell me in the comments, and subscribe to Factuality for more space, science and nature.

